on_service.py` calls itself \"the one path every model call takes\", but in the coordinator cycle only the adjudicator goes through it: the last 40 session logs in `docs/iteration/` are all `role: ADJUDICATE` (both reviewers confirmed). Builders are Claude Code sub-agents of the coordinator session. Sol and Terra launch through `coordinator-tools/sol_review.sh` and `terra_author.sh` straight to `codex exec`. The leg itself runs as `claude -p`. None of those are recorded.\r\n\r\n**Size of the gap.** Leg 3 (2026-10-11), read from its transcripts and counted once per message id. Revision 1 summed repeated records of the same message, which doubled the totals. The coordinator: about 151k output tokens and 33.5M cache-read tokens. Nine `kit-builder` sub-agents: about 564k output. One `Plan` sub-agent: about 51k. Builders were about 74% of the leg's Claude output (all sub-agents about 80%), none of it in the kit's records. Sol and Terra usage is unmeasured.\r\n\r\n**Where the data is.** Claude Code writes each sub-agent's transcript under `<session>/subagents/agent-*.jsonl`, beside a `.meta.json` naming the agent type, its task and its `spawnDepth`. A message's usage appears in several records and must be counted once. Where depth-2 transcripts land is unverified. WI-800 (queued) already owns the durable invocation store and an idempotent usage ledger.\r\n\r\n### Proposal\r\n\r\n1. **Route Sol and Terra through `session_service`**, as `coordinator_adjudicate.py` already routes the adjudicator. The launch scripts keep their sandbox, effort and HEAD/status checks but call the service. **Corrected in revision 32** (Astra): the service's `record` commits the session log in the call's root (`agent_common.commit_telemetry`), and the adjudicator's path runs from the lane on purpose, so a recorded Sol or Terra call moves the lane's HEAD and the wrapper reports it as the model's edit (exit 3). So the change check runs where the model returns, between the service's `act` and its `record`, and the log commit is not counted as an edit. **Corrected in revision 36** (both reviewers): revision 32 went on to say that two parallel reviewers commit their logs one after the other \"through the one writer\". No such writer exists yet. `commit_telemetry` serializes nothing: two `record`s in one worktree contend for git's index lock, and the loser's log is left uncommitted. The one writer is WI-800's store, and even serialized, one reviewer's log commit moves HEAD under the other's change check. That case needs two service-routed reviewers on one lane, which arrives with item 7's Gemini slot; today reviewer B is a sub-agent. A call run from the primary checkout, as every scope critique is, would commit its log on trunk, which `coordinator_adjudicate.lane_refusal` refuses the adjudicator for exactly that reason. So P2's spec settles two things: where a call run outside a lane records its log, and that a log commit another call makes on the same lane is not an edit (both records after both checks, or a check that discounts session-log commits).\r\n2. **Ingest Claude sub-agent usage under WI-800's ledger contract.** Read the leg's transcript and its sub-agent transcripts. Count once per message id. Attribute each invocation exactly once (by invocation identity, so a repeated close-out or a resumed transcript adds nothing). Write through the service's one writer. Verify where nested transcripts land before claiming coverage of nested agents (revision 37: planners, builders and reviewers may now spawn sub-agents, so P2 covers nested agents).\r\n3. **Verify the alternative.** If a `claude -p` session's final usage includes its own sub-agents, builders could launch through the service directly. Unverified.\r\n4. **Use the rows.** Per landed WI: builder, reviewer, author and adjudicator tokens and wall-clock beside its review rounds. That turns the re-measure (phase 4) into a query.\r\n\r\n**Trade-off.** The transcript format belongs to Claude Code and can change. Keep the reader in one adapter (`session_adapters`), refusing loudly on an unknown shape.\r\n\r\n**Downstream.** Step 1 touches this repo's coordinator tools. Step 2 adds an adapter to a shipped module: one RESYNC entry.\r\n\r\n**Owner calls (ruled; the rulings section governs):**\r\n\r\n- Confirm or overrule routing Sol and Terra through the session service.\r\n- Confirm or overrule ingesting sub-agent usage under WI-800's ledger, ahead of WI-800's other parts if needed.\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
