{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$v = Get-Content '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-22c-leg13/crit1/WI-961-plan-critique-1.md'; \"'$v[0]; $v | Select-String '\"'\"'^VERDICT:|''^- '\"\\\\[MAJOR\\\\]'; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"Reviewed: 381e77d4080e30c3449809cd86de076bb3bcb051\r\n\r\n- [MAJOR] DevStg-Tests -> P3/P5, decisions 2 and 5, and “Bounds and risks: A message in flight” permanently omit later \r\noutput-token updates to a message already passed by the cursor. The plan itself establishes that repeated assistant \r\nrecords commonly increase output_tokens, and P6 invokes ingest while the coordinator session is still running; \r\nsub-agents may also still run. A later ingest only visits messages after the cursor, so it cannot restore the missing \r\nusage even after the transcript finishes. Measuring this in P8 does not close D4's requirement that contributions sum \r\nto usage over every unique message id, and the declared exclusion is not honest for the cycle's supported live \r\nclose-out route. -> Plan a finalization boundary that records only immutable, completed message usage and leaves \r\nunfinished messages eligible for later recording, or obtain a judged specification amendment before building the \r\nweaker accounting promise; add an initial/updated-record/resumed-ingest check whose contributions equal the completed \r\ntranscript. -> @WI-961-planner\r\n- [MAJOR] DevStg-Tests -> P5 and decision 4 derive the log filename's stamp from the last counted message to second \r\nprecision, then permanently refuse a distinct contribution with the same name. Distinct appended messages can have \r\ntimestamps in the same second in provider-written transcripts. After recording the first contribution, the second is \r\nrefused on every retry of the now-complete transcript because its source timestamp never changes. The planned \r\nsame-name test proves refusal but leaves D4's appended-message recording and interrupted-run recovery unsatisfied; \r\ndistinct contribution keys do not resolve the filename collision. -> Plan collision-free contribution filenames within \r\nthe standard call-log contract, retaining actual source timestamps in the log, and test two message ranges under one \r\ninvocation whose last timestamps share a second: both contributions survive and a repeated ingest adds nothing. -> \r\n@WI-961-planner\r\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=2\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
